# Two-Player Layout Redesign — Implementation Plan

> **For Claude:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.

**Goal:** Replace the flex-wrap role card layout with a fixed-zone 3-column CSS grid for the crew (all_advisors) and CO (decision_maker) player views in 2-player mode.

**Architecture:** The player-view template branches on player role: `all_advisors` renders a 3-column grid with fixed intel/decision zones per column; `decision_maker` renders the same 3-column grid (read-only mirrors) plus a full-width CO decision bar at the bottom. A new `BoardColumnComponent` wraps each role's intel and decision content into fixed vertical zones. The existing `RoleCardComponent` gains a `readonly` mode for CO mirrors. A new `CoDecisionBarComponent` handles the CO's option picker with recommendation badges.

**Tech Stack:** Angular 21 (standalone, signals, OnPush), CSS @layer in `components-player-view.css`, Vitest for unit tests.

**Design doc:** `docs/plans/2026-03-22-two-player-layout-design.md`

**Worktree:** `.worktrees/two-player-layout` on branch `feature/two-player-layout`

